 "observations": [
  "body: the first page of the commentary: a double rule, heavy over thin, across the head of the page; the title, set in a large condensed bold type; a short rule; the head of the notes on chapter 3, «Ad» and «caput» in small capitals; the print numbers no lines in the commentary.",
  "body L7-L14: the formulas stand as printed, their labels in bold; the words «seu chorda» of (α), (β), (δ), (ε) and (ζ) stand in one column.",
  "body L11: in (ε) the second term under the root is printed 2R/4, without a square; the side of the decagon, chorda 36° = √(R² + (R/2)²) − R/2, asks for (2R/4)²; kept as printed.",
  "body L15: «Halma, t. I.» is printed with a full stop before the line break.",
  "notes_right L2: the sign between the two products is printed −; the chord of the sum is crd (p + q) = [crd p crd (180° − q) + crd q crd (180° − p)] / 2R, and with − the rule gives crd (p − q), the rule (η) of the text; kept as printed.",
  "notes_right L1-L2: Nallino's addenda et emendanda in Part II (p. XXI; AB01-PDF0438-body-L017) put + for the − in the numerator of the fraction, «+ crd q crd (180° — p)». With crd x = 2R sin (x/2) and crd (180° − x) = 2R cos (x/2), crd p crd (180° − q) + crd q crd (180° − p) = 4R² sin ((p + q)/2) = 2R crd (p + q), the rule of the sum of two arcs; with the printed −, the fraction gives crd (p − q). The printed − is kept."
 ],
